caption: Character Drive Sheet Assembly
rule: character-drive-sheet-assembly

At campaign start, assemble each character's active Drive sheet from:

The campaign's Campaign Drives.

The first N Drives from every active Domain source.

The first N Drives from every active World source.

The first N Drives from every active Pantheon source.

The first N Drives from every active Culture source.

The first N Drives from any additional active source categories.

Any required Secondary Choice attached to an active Drive.

The campaign decides whether N is the same for every source category or differs by category.

A character may be eligible for several possible sources while using only the number permitted by the campaign. The player selects the active source or sources.

Active sources and Secondary Choices persist until the player voluntarily changes them under the campaign's change rules. No fictional event, loss of membership, loss of powers, death of a patron, collapse of a nation, magical compulsion, or GM declaration automatically changes them.

Drive internalization is an Isekai-specific legacy mechanic and is not assumed by this framework.
